# Demo-local build/venv/output artifacts. Only the tour/wild sources,
# render scripts, the rendered PNGs under renders*/ and the two
# renderer-free lanes' SVG sheets (renders-uv/montage-uv.svg and
# renders-mc/plate-density.svg — text, so they diff) are tracked. The
# UV lane's per-face cells live under out/uv/ and are not: there are
# ~1000 of them, and the sheet is the artifact worth keeping. The MC
# lane's own out/mc/ is the same story with one file.
# (`out/` matches at any depth, so demos/wild/out/ is covered too.)
tour/target/
wild/target/
out/
.venv/
target-demo/
renders-freecad/*.fail.txt
# out/ already covers the render staging trees (out/stage-renders*/)
# and the per-scene FreeCAD logs; spelled out because they are the
# only place an in-flight pass exists.
out/freecad-logs/

# THE GUI LANE IS AN ALLOWLIST, and it is the only lane here that needs
# to be. A CLEAN pass needs no rule at all: it stages under out/gui,
# which `out/` above already covers at any depth, and publishes PNG and
# nothing else. This is about the other passes. It is the one lane that
# drives a real application — an X server, a window, a screen grabber —
# so what an interrupted or failed one can leave beside the cells is
# open-ended, and the re-baseline action runs `git add -A --
# demos/renders-gui/` on every hosted run: whatever is there is
# COMMITTED, and then registers as drift on every run after that.
# Naming the scratch instead would mean naming it before it exists. The
# cost is the loud half of the trade: a new kind of cell that belongs in
# the repo is not committed until it is admitted here.
renders-gui/*
!renders-gui/*.png
